secure-exec: make Xvfb RandR report the -screen geometry, not the 1280x1024 default

third_party/xserver/ is large and not tracked in VCS (it is fetched/reconstructed
out of band), so the secure-exec X-server source patches live as patch files here.

Bug: `vfbInitializeScreenInfo()` copies `defaultScreenInfo` (1280x1024) and seeds the
RandR CRTC geometry from those defaults BEFORE `-screen WxHxD` is parsed. The parse
(`ddxProcessArgument`) then updates only `vfbScreens[n].width/height`, so the core
screen and the framebuffer use the configured size, but `crtcs[].width/height` keep
the 1280x1024 default. `vfbRandRInit()` builds the RandR mode/output/CRTC from those
stale CRTC dims, so XRRGetScreenResourcesCurrent / XRRGetMonitors report 1280x1024.

Impact: RandR-aware clients (GTK's GdkMonitor geometry, lxpanel's percent-width /
strut panels) size themselves to the phantom 1024 dimension. On a 640x480 screen the
LXDE panel was laid out 26x1024 and painted entirely off the visible area => black
screen. With the fix the panel is sized to the real screen and renders.

Fix: after the `-screen` sscanf, drive the CRTC geometry from the parsed screen size
so RandR is consistent with the core protocol and the framebuffer.

After applying, rebuild + re-apply wasm-opt --fpcast-emu (scripts/link-xvfb.sh now
does this automatically):
    scripts/link-xvfb.sh

--- a/hw/vfb/InitOutput.c
+++ b/hw/vfb/InitOutput.c
@@ -353,6 +353,22 @@ ddxProcessArgument(int argc, char *argv[], int i)
             FatalError("Invalid screen configuration %s for -screen %d\n",
                        argv[i + 2], screenNum);
         }

+        /* The RandR CRTCs were initialized from the 1280x1024 default in
+         * vfbInitializeScreenInfo() BEFORE this -screen parse. The core screen and framebuffer now
+         * use the configured WxH, but the CRTC/output geometry is still the stale default, so RandR
+         * (XRRGetScreenResourcesCurrent / XRRGetMonitors) reports 1280x1024. RandR-aware clients
+         * (GTK monitor geometry, lxpanel struts/percent-width panels) then mis-size to that phantom
+         * resolution. Drive the CRTC geometry from the configured screen so RandR is consistent. */
+        {
+            int crtcIndex;
+            for (crtcIndex = 0; crtcIndex < vfbScreens[screenNum].numCrtcs; ++crtcIndex) {
+                vfbScreens[screenNum].crtcs[crtcIndex].width =
+                    vfbScreens[screenNum].width;
+                vfbScreens[screenNum].crtcs[crtcIndex].height =
+                    vfbScreens[screenNum].height;
+            }
+        }
+
         lastScreen = screenNum;
         return 3;
     }
